PATIENT EDUCATION

Treatment Explanation: You have contracted a very common parasitic infection called Trichomoniasis, which causes severe inflammation, swelling, and that specific frothy discharge. It is not an ascending pelvic infection, so your uterus and tubes are safe. The single large dose of antibiotics will eradicate the parasite quickly. It is absolutely crucial that you do not consume a single drop of alcohol for 48 hours after taking this medication, or you will vomit violently.
Actionable Steps: Take the oral medication immediately with food. Strictly no alcohol for 48 hours. Use the numbing gel sparingly on the outside tissue, and ensure your partner gets treated immediately.

